<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shibam</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shibam is a walled town in the Wadi Hadramawt of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a>, famous for its densely packed mud-brick tower houses, many of them five to eleven storeys high and dating mainly from the 16th century onwards. Often called the '<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manhattan">Manhattan</a> of the desert', it was an ancient capital of Hadramawt and a station on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caravan-trade">caravan routes</a>. It is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shibam.jpg" alt="Shibam" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bkar6190 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D9%85%D8%AF%D9%8A%D9%86%D8%A9_%D8%B4%D8%A8%D8%A7%D9%85_%D8%AD%D8%B6%D8%B1%D9%85%D9%88%D8%AA.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
